{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 138, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a residual shortcut where no direct input-output path exists gives far larger gains than replacing an existing op (exps 21, 27-30 vs 22-24)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty direct edge adds a new path, whereas replacing an existing op only swaps one (exps 83, 86 vs 84, 85)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With node1->output also absent, deleting edge 3 removes most or all routes to the output (exps 32, 36)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 3 is empty, edge 5 may be the only route to the output, so removing it can disconnect the cell (exp 68)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the direct edge, edge 0 feeds every remaining path, so removing it is catastrophic (exp 74)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping a 1x1 conv for a 3x3 adds little compared with adding the first learnable op on a parameter-free edge (exp 54 vs 51-53)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "In skip-dominated, conv-poor cells, another identity path degrades the cell instead of providing a useful residual (exp 25)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a conv with skip in an already skip-heavy cell removes scarce learnable capacity (exp 60 vs 61-63)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connec